  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Treasure, a narrative poem about personal change, uses the images of Jiffy Pop popcorn (instructions in Japanese) as a metaphor for a turning point in a woman's life and suggests an imminent need for change everywhere."--Women's Studio Workshop website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This edition is printed on handmade abaca paper with silkscreen and moku hanga. Moku hanga is a traditional Japanese woodblock method that uses waterbased pigments and a baren for printing by hand. The text is Optima 24 point lead type, handset and printed on a No. 3 Vandercook."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in an edition of 35 copies and signed by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Bound in brown silk, with stylistic drawing of popcorn on front cover. Accordion-folded paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC copy has copy no. 29, signed by artist.</subfield>
